# Where code belongs

- **SIG-Stakeholder-Database** (`https://github.com/51monharr15/SIG-Stakeholder-Database`): only Stroke Improvement Group **stakeholder database** work (e.g. `lusers.php` / MySQL stakeholder data).
- **MeetingScheduler** (`https://github.com/51monharr15/MeetingScheduler`): Meet Scheduler and anything about scheduling meetings that is **not** the SIG stakeholder database.
- If a change is about SIG stakeholders and that database, it goes in the SIG repo. If it is about something else, it does **not**.

Do not add Meet Scheduler files, docs, or branches into SIG-Stakeholder-Database. Do not treat Obsidian copies named `SIG-Stakeholder-Database-*-meet-*` as the canonical Meet home — use `MeetingScheduler`.
